  "4_decision": {
    "recommended": "inject_writes_through_to_ontology_json",
    "rationale": [
      "Production resolve order is L1 \u2192 L2 (ontology.json) \u2192 L3 (DB). For any name present in ontology.json, live merges never reach a verdict.",
      "Write-through keeps the offline/test path (no DB) identical to production for ontology-named ingredients \u2014 tests already load ontology.json.",
      "DB-before-L2 would fix drift but split offline tests from production unless tests always run against a DB fixture.",
      "L2 regenerated from DB after each inject is equivalent if regeneration is mandatory in the inject CLI and CI fails when ontology.json is stale \u2014 write-through is the simpler invariant (inject is the single writer)."
    ],
    "rejected_alternatives": {
      "db_before_l2": "Fixes runtime drift but makes ontology.json a cache of last resort; CI/unit tests without Supabase would silently see stale L2 or miss rows.",
      "l2_regenerated_from_db": "Works if enforced, but two-step (inject then export) is easy to skip; write-through folds the export into the inject transaction."
    },
    "item12_audit": "Add L2-vs-L3 drift check: for every live source=ontology (and every live row whose canonical_name is in ontology.json), diff verdict-relevant true flags; fail or ticket when live_true and l2_false on allergen/species/animal_origin. Diff by name, not aggregate count.",
    "new_item": "Logged as Item 41 (P0): docs/item41_l2_l3_dual_store_authority.md \u2014 dual stores need one declared authority + L2\u2194L3 drift test (step-1: 1738 live ontology rows, 44 with verdict-relevant drift)."
  },
